WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:05.400
Module 03 · Course 2 · Organise · For entrepreneurs
Structure, Governance & Accountability

2
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.800
Decide who will do the work, who decides and who you answer to, while it is easy to set up.

3
00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:30.615
This module helps you design the work before the job titles: which functions you need, who decides what, how governance stays separate from daily management and who you answer to. It answers: how will we organise, decide and stay accountable?

4
00:00:31.015 --> 00:00:31.615
Why set this up early

5
00:00:31.615 --> 00:00:38.400
1. Structure is easy to shape while you are small and hard to change later.

6
00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:44.074
2. Unclear roles between co-founders are a common source of early conflict.

7
00:00:44.074 --> 00:00:51.859
3. Funders and partners want to see who decides and who holds you to account.

8
00:00:52.259 --> 00:01:01.959
What you will work through: 3.1 From work to structure · 3.2 Organisational structures and organigrams · 3.3 Governance structures by legal form · 3.4 Board and management responsibilities · 3.5 Roles and role descriptions · 3.6 Decision rights and delegation of authority · 3.7 RACI and process ownership · 3.8 Accountability and reporting lines · 3.9 Coordination and internal communication · 3.10 Recap: Structure, Governance & Accountability

9
00:01:02.359 --> 00:01:02.959
What you will have

10
00:01:02.959 --> 00:01:09.374
1. A map of the functions your strategy needs and a simple organisation chart.

11
00:01:09.374 --> 00:01:15.048
2. Role cards, approval limits and a RACI that make responsibilities explicit.

12
00:01:15.048 --> 00:01:21.722
3. A governance set-up and a meeting rhythm that keep you accountable.

13
00:01:22.122 --> 00:01:22.722
Working through it

14
00:01:22.722 --> 00:01:29.507
1. Work through it with your co-founders; agreeing roles together is part of the value.

15
00:01:29.507 --> 00:01:35.552
2. Include work you have not started yet, so the structure can grow.

16
00:01:35.552 --> 00:01:42.967
3. Our example bakery shows how two co-founders and an advisory group share decisions.

17
00:01:43.567 --> 00:01:45.567
You create: Your Structure & Accountability Pack: functions, chart, governance, roles, delegation, RACI and rhythm.

18
00:01:45.567 --> 00:01:50.367
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

19
00:01:51.867 --> 00:01:54.967
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
